      "description": "The Fillmore Auditorium, formerly the Majestic Ballroom, which the promoter Charles Sullivan booked through the postwar years. It was also the first address of Muhammad Mosque No. 26 and the mosque's home again by 1973. Identified in 2024 as eligible for local landmark, California Register or National Register designation.",
